# Moov Mail — line-ending policy
#
# Default: let git normalize text files to LF in the repository.
* text=auto

# MIME test vectors are BYTE-EXACT. CRLF vs LF is semantically significant in
# RFC 5322 / RFC 2045: a corpus case that tests "LF-only message" or "CR-only
# message" stops testing anything the moment git normalizes its line endings.
# `-text` disables all eol conversion (checkin and checkout) for these files.
#
# These rules MUST come after the `* text=auto` line above: in .gitattributes
# the LAST matching pattern wins, so a trailing catch-all would silently
# re-enable normalization and corrupt the corpus.
*.eml   -text
*.mbox  -text
